# General Architecture Rules - Arcanovi Project

## Core Communication Principles

- Assistant responds in German during conversations
- **ALL code, variable names, comments, functions, directory names, documentation, and structural elements MUST be written in English**
- Technical terminology is used precisely regarding Django, React, PostgreSQL, Docker, Nginx, and Feature-Driven Design

## Project Architecture Overview

### Feature-Driven Design (FDD)
The entire system follows **Feature-Driven Design** principles:
- **Django Backend**: Features organized as independent Django apps under `backend/api/apps/`
- **React Frontend**: Features organized in `frontend/src/features/` with Atomic Design patterns
- Each feature maintains complete independence with clear boundaries
- Cross-feature communication only through well-defined interfaces

### Technology Stack
- **Backend**: Django + PostgreSQL + JWT Authentication
- **Frontend**: React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS
- **Infrastructure**: Docker + Nginx + Docker Compose
- **Real-time**: Server-Sent Events (SSE) for streaming (optional)

## Django Backend Architecture (backend Service)

### Feature Organization
- Each feature = one Django app in `backend/api/apps/`
- Apps follow aspect-based separation (see rules for Django Backend Architecture)
- API-only backend - no template rendering, no Django Admin
- JWT authentication as the only authentication model

### Key Specifications
- PostgreSQL as central database with optimized indexing
- Database-based session management (no Redis dependency)
- Gunicorn as WSGI server for container deployment
- Server-Sent Events (SSE) support for real-time streaming (optional)
- RESTful API design under `/api/` endpoints

### Dependencies
- Django & Django REST Framework
- psycopg2 (PostgreSQL Adapter)
- gunicorn (WSGI Server)
- django-environ (environment management)
- djangorestframework-simplejwt (JWT authentication)
- Background tasks handled by Django's built-in mechanisms or lightweight alternatives

## React Frontend Architecture (frontend Service)

### Feature Organization
- Features in `frontend/src/features/<FeatureName>/` with strict directory structure
- Atomic Design: atoms/, molecules/, organisms/ within each feature
- TypeScript enforcement for all components and services
- Mandatory internationalization - no hardcoded strings (see rules for React Feature Development)

### Key Specifications
- Vite as build tool and development server
- React Router for client-side routing
- React Query or SWR for data fetching
- Tailwind CSS for styling (configured in `tailwind.config.js`)
- Design System integration with component reuse
- SSE integration for real-time updates (optional, see rules for React SSE Integration)

### Dependencies
- React + TypeScript
- Vite (build tool)
- React Router (routing)
- React Query/SWR (data fetching)
- Tailwind CSS (styling)
- react-i18next (internationalization)
- ESLint + Prettier (code quality)

## Services Integration & Communication

### Nginx Reverse Proxy
- Forwards requests between frontend and backend services
- Serves static files and media from Docker volumes
- Optimized SSE configuration for real-time streaming (optional, see rules for Infrastructure & DevOps)

### API Communication
- RESTful API design with versioning (`/api/v1/`)
- JWT authentication for all protected endpoints
- CORS configuration for cross-origin requests
- Swagger/OpenAPI documentation (drf-spectacular)

### Real-time Features (Optional)
- Server-Sent Events (SSE) for streaming responses
- JWT authentication in SSE connections via polyfill
- Event-driven architecture for feature communication

